{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310549,"nonce":"5BBUfSIxE5Ue5+M5MB0+JuMlwZg=","title":"FIXED in commit 5186eb8 (workflow w269anak1). Top-level .mir.cache key now folds transitive import-set hash + RAYZOR_BUILD_ID into ...","message":"**Status: FIXED (preventive)** in commit `5186eb8` (workflow `w269anak1`).\n\n`compute_import_set_hash` in `compiler/src/ir/blade.rs` walks the entry source's transitive import graph, resolves each `import x.y.Z;` qname under `manifest_dirs`, hashes (qname, file bytes), and recurses. MAX_VISITS=4096 caps pathological input. `compiler::BUILD_ID = env!(\"RAYZOR_BUILD_ID\")` is folded into the same hash. Cache file format unchanged; stale caches naturally miss on the first u64 compare.\n\nThree verified-fixed classes of cascade-busting change:\n1. Content edits to transitively-imported modules deeper than depth-2.\n2. Compiler rebuilds (`RAYZOR_BUILD_ID` bump).\n3. Re-export changes that reroute import resolution.\n\nVerifier independently confirmed: editing `nue/sampling/ArgmaxSampler.hx` (depth-3, beyond legacy depth-2 mtime walk) changed `import_hash` from `0x9d54313b98d043be` to `0xd2688cf691ad4901` and bumped `Main.mir.cache` mtime, proving the transitive walk fires.\n\n**Scope note**: this is PREVENTIVE — it does not address specific stale-id bugs in cached MIR maps (e.g. the three iface sibling maps identified by workflow `w7c228293`: `import_interface_method_names`, `import_interface_method_return_types`, `import_interface_extends` — those still need their own BLADE persistence per `bugs_trap_stub_cascade`). But with this fix, any future stale-id bug whose trigger is an import-set change can no longer hide behind a hash-collision cache hit.\n\nKnown non-blocking limitations:\n- DFS not BFS despite comment (cosmetic; Vec::pop is LIFO)\n- Wildcard imports `import pkg.*;` silently contribute nothing\n- MAX_VISITS=4096 silently truncates large graphs (no warning)\n- Only walks `manifest_dirs`, not `rpkg_source_dirs` ([dependencies]-consumed modules fall back to per-module `.blade` BUILD_ID guard)\n\n\n\nThe BLADE cache at `\u003cproject\u003e/.rayzor/cache/Main.mir.cache` is consulted via `src/main.rs:1054-1078` BEFORE the compilation pipeline runs. If the source hash matches, the cached MIR is loaded and executed directly without going through:\n\n- `restore_cached_maps` (where the woa9qquvk Fix 1 interface_vtables qname re-resolve lives)\n- `fixup_stale_cross_module_refs`\n- `fixup_stale_constructor_ids`\n- `fixup_stale_stdlib_function_ids` (the woa9qquvk Fix 2 stdlib fixup)\n- Any future fixup\n\nSo if the cache was written by a save-session whose import set DIFFERS from the load-session (e.g. user added/removed an import between runs, or the BLADE cache was created at a different commit), the cached MIR's external function id references point to stale ids that no fixup pass can reach.\n\n\nWorkflow `woa9qquvk` confirmed STEP 2 of `/tmp/trap_repro/repro.sh` still reproduces the cascade EVEN after landing both Fix 1 (vtable qname re-resolve) and Fix 2 (stdlib function id fixup). The remaining stale id was traced to one of:\n\n- `import_function_param_iface_names`\n- `external_function_param_types`\n- CallDirect targets in cached MIR not present in `external_function_names`\n\nBut none of those fixups will ever run on a cache-hit code path. So the cascade can be \"fixed\" in compilation.rs and still reproduce because the cached MIR bypasses the fix entirely.\n\n\nTwo complementary options:\n\n1. **Invalidate cache on import-set hash mismatch**. Add the resolved import set (qualified names sorted) to the cache key. Any change to imports invalidates the cache and forces a fresh compilation pipeline + all fixups. Cleanest.\n\n2. **Run fixups on cached MIR before execution**. The cache-hit path at `src/main.rs:1054-1078` reads `Main.mir.cache`, deserialises the MIR, then jumps to execution. Insert a fixup pass between deserialisation and execution: re-resolve external function ids via the freshly-built `stdlib_function_name_map` + `external_function_names`. Cheaper if cache hit rate matters; more code paths to maintain.\n\nOption (1) is preferred. The cache is meant as a speed-up for unchanged programs; an import-set change is exactly the kind of structural shift that should invalidate.\n\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p /tmp/trap_repro/work \u0026\u0026 cd /tmp/trap_repro/work\ncat \u003eMain.hx \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nimport nue.sampling.TemperatureSampler;  // or rayzor.concurrent.WorkerPool\nclass Main { static function main() { trace(\"hi\"); } }\nEOF\ncat \u003erayzor.toml \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n[project]\nname = \"trap_repro\"\nentry = \"Main.hx\"\nEOF\nrayzor run Main.hx\nsed -i '' '/^import/d' Main.hx\nrayzor run Main.hx  # silently exits 0 or SIGSEGVs depending on which fixup is bypassed\n```\n\nThe cascade fires when the cache was written with one external-function set and the program is now loading with a different one.\n\n\nInstrument codegen entry of `LlamaModel.forwardIds` (or whichever function the cascade fires in) to print every `CallDirect` target `IrFunctionId`. Run with cache cold (STEP 1 — no cache hit, full pipeline runs) AND with cache warm (STEP 2 — cache-hit fast path). Diff the two ID streams. The id whose resolved real function differs between them is the culprit map entry that needs either fixup or cache invalidation.\n\n\n- [[bugs-trap-stub-cascade]] — the original family\n- [[bugs-int64-multivar-stub-replace]] — the established fix pattern (per-map fixup_stale_*_ids)\n- [[bugs-forward-ref-stub-unresolved]] — earlier cross-file dispatch fix\n- [[bugs-llama-8b-sigsegv-at-gen-start]] — 8B SIGSEGV is hypothesised to be the same root cause; blocked on this fix\n- [[project-qmatmul-threaded]] — `nue.Linear` WorkerPool integration blocked on this\n- [[project-llama-chat-temperature-penalty]] — `nue.sampling.TemperatureSampler` swap blocked on this\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_cache_hit_fast_path_bypasses_fixups` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}